<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6756"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Featherw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Featherw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 5:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree Skiller. Like yourself, I suspect he is up to no good.  He is definately not going to give us any clues to his next plan.  <BR> <BR>Susan?  He says she is his prize.   <BR> <BR>Johno could be right...There is a Susan who is a co-anchor at KAKE right?  But why would he tell us the name of his next victim?  If he actually has a specific person in mind as his next victim, you can bet he won&#39;t give anyone the correct name of the person, but rather &#40;I think..&#41; he would give a false name of a person to MISLEAD as he always seems to do.  Naming a name is just another way he is misleading IMO.   <BR> <BR>He may have a next victim in mind.  But..I can almost be sure SUSAN is not her or his name.  <BR> <BR>If you need to get a list of specfic persons who live in the area you mentioned, I would suggest something complete...like a cross reference list...census bureau doc...something that is pretty recent.  If you feel the area you mentioned is his next area to strike at a victim, checking a cross reference for names of persons might be a shot.. <BR> <BR>But...I would not look for someone named SUSAN.  <BR> <BR>I think he might be bluffing too.  But...before he started presenting driver&#39;s licenses of his last victims just last year, he never BLUFFED, never gave hints, never gave warnings...he just killed without taunting beforehand.  Taunting came afterward.  Makes me wonder. <BR> <BR>Thanks.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
