<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7153"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 12:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here is the stable rumor storie: <BR> <BR> The gossip I heard over and over was that the BTK was the member of the <BR>&#62; family who owned Bridle and Saddle, and that he was never arrested <BR>&#62; because of the family&#39;s money and influence. <BR> <BR> <BR><a href="http://groups.google.dk/groups?q=%22%2BStables%22%2B%2Bbtk%2B%2Bwichita&amp;hl=en&amp;lr=&amp;safe=off&amp;selm=stu9c.14941%24mf.3572%40okepread05&amp;rnum=1" target=_top>http://groups.google.dk/groups?q=%22&#43;Stables%22&#43;%2 Bbtk&#43;%2Bwichita&amp;hl=en&amp;lr=&amp;safe=off&amp;selm=stu9c.1494 1%24mf.3572%40okepread05&amp;rnum=1</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
