<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7168"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Richerich<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Richerich<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 3:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Amateur slueths notwithstanding, some of these posts are nonetheless very interesting. As such without useful info from LE....speculation runs rampant thruout these message posts. Reading far fetched implications into every minute detail from A to Z leads one to understand why LE does not let loose with details from their investigations. Btk is probably fascinated and amused by all the details written that are so far off the wall that he wonders when the time will actually come when someone whether in LE or the public trip him up in to being caught. Until then when LE have the evidence to make an arrest or he is tripped up in public communicating, then BTK is safe from apphrehension. unfortunately insulated by armchair uninformed detectives that read farfetched innuendo into every last piece of info whether authenticated or not. Being critical of my opinion is irrelevant. I have not nor will I use random speculation about the case but depend on the facts be them as they are gleaned from the professional investigators and what they choose to release to the public. I would imagine LE types close to the case keep the pertinent info non public for reasons that all these so called detectives could not understand. I do not claim to understand either, but common sense dictates to me LE is not withholding pertinent info just for grins to prolong the investigation, but to keep the public informed while tightening the noose around any suspects they may have. and one last thought: I will not ever believe LE would cover up a SK just because the family had money or influence. In my mind that again is absolutely, insanely, hysterically, preposterous. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7168-->
<!--Post: 7170--><!--Time: 1108252898-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7170"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 4:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->wow. My posts have been taken down for far less agregious comments than that!  <BR> <BR>Is there much oxygen up there on that pedestal in the sky, Richerich? Obviously not, or you would actually have the capacity for abstract thought. It would be one thing if you spewed anything useful to go along with your huge dose of criticism and sarcasm....Weak, onesided, and negative. Bet you&#39;re a charming guy to live with! <BR> <BR>&#34;Absolutely, insanely, hysterically, preposterous&#34; - all used to describe your contribution here! <BR> <BR>Best Regards, Lily<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7170-->
<!--Post: 7171--><!--Time: 1108255192-->
