<!--Post: 7248--><!--Time: 1108325348-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7248"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Richerich<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Richerich<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 12:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Knowing how easy it is for investigators or owners of websites to see who is posting anyone in their right mind would never imply they are or claim to be a murderer.The 2 previous posters are absolutely wrong. When I applied for posting privileges I furnished my true identity and information. Heck I want the SK caught......I just dont believe that all these posting from folks claiming insight into this and that whatever the detail might help much. I would like to think LE, if monitoring these postings, can see thru the levels of imagination it takes to dream up some minute detail as to waste valuable LE resources chasing Wag the Dog. Again criticize me, my grammar and anything else folks have from me. Its again strange the sleuths thruout this website get angry when challenging some of their off the wall, out of the box thinkings, call it what you will. I choose to trust LE in their endeavours of catching the murderer instead of dwelling on hypothetical dreams as portrayed by some of the posters who  summarize their points by being critical of a poster who may not agree with all the rubbish that some posters concoct whether true or not. Not naming any posters, nor being critical of any named poster still does not warrant attacks on any individual. Because one feels some of the ramblings and innuendos of posters in this message board are to say the least.......bizarre... does not make the one who questions some of the goofy notions an enemy. If I had some inside LE info I might think differently, but without that I will still trust LE is close to an arrest. Everything else is what I would call poster aggrandisement.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7248-->
<!--Post: 7250--><!--Time: 1108327182-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7250"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 12:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think this Website and the discussion forum are a great idea. Many SK cases that are solved are solved because of tips from the public. The public gives LE a landfill full of donkey kaka to sort through, sure, but there are good leads in there too.  If someone in Wichita views this site simply because it exists, and comes across a post that jogs their memory and they give LE the tip that breaks the case, then the online circus is worth it, IMHO.  No one is twisting our arms to read the posts and put up our own posts, it&#39;s on our own time.   <BR> <BR>Look at it another way -- before the age of Web discussion boards like this, individuals would phone or write to LE with every idea they had related to the case.  By discussing ideas online, people might realize that their idea is way, way off and that it&#39;s not worth bothering LE.  Or, through discussion their suspicions might find some justification.   <BR> <BR>The Website&#39;s a new concept.  I wouldn&#39;t give up on it that easily.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7250-->
<!--Post: 7251--><!--Time: 1108327370-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7251"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 12:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->First off, the name rich e rich. The double thing. <BR> <BR>Then a single statement saying pre post erous. the post in the middle. <BR> <BR>Then in the second post he starts out calm and amused, but gets wound up and his sentence structure begins to lapse into btk-speak stating, as if fact, that LE is privy to information that we can not imagine &#40;and thus he shouldn&#39;t know&#41;, but he can&#39;t quite lower himself to our level. But then he states that he doesn&#39;t know. But says it very formally and slights it off. He repeats various versions of amateur sleuths three of four times as if it were an insult to him personally, when we know there are several professionals working this board.  <BR> <BR>There are two consecutive lines where he mentions getting tripped up in communication, almost out of context, as if he was thinking about it.  <BR> <BR>he uses an almost third person style that [BTK] uses. <BR> <BR>At the end he gets real pissed about the insinuation that big money might be the secret behind [BTK&#39;s] illusiveness, as if he is trying to convince himself. <BR> <BR>Then finishes his tirade with pre post erous.&#40;who says preposterous anymore&#41;. <BR> <BR>Then he starts off his third one all paranoid again, insisting that he is not affected by critisism, but then, why is he even bothering to talk? in the entirety of the three posts, the only point he makes is that he is upset that we are speculating and reading between the lines, instead of playing by the rules. The rules being that [BTK] leaves a specific clue and we are supposed to find it, in the proper sequence, and interpret it in the way [BTK] expects us to interpret it. We aren&#39;t supposed to notice the Freudian slips &#40;like &#39;richer rich&#39; getting his shorts in a knot over the insinuation [BTK&#39;s] family might be paying off the athourities to keep [BTK] out of prison, when ricci knows that it is [BTK&#39;s] cunning that makes him...like the wind&#41;.  <BR> <BR>And at the end of his argument...what technicality? Does mr. rich think that the WPD is going to overlook all of the loose evidence [BTK] left lying and floating around all those times when he was stoned or ran out of thorozine and escaped from the estate, I mean got out of the house. The minute the PD has a name or number they are going to bust [BTK] and his family, I mean anyone who might have been harboring him. But I&#39;m really sure they will read them their rights. <BR> <BR>All of this makes me suspect that richerich just might be [the alledged BTK]. But mostly it&#39;s because BTK quit writing the other day and this shmo just shows up out of nowhere and starts typing like a loony-toon.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7251-->
<!--Post: 7253--><!--Time: 1108329347-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7253"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Richerich<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Richerich<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 1:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->As bizarre as the previous post is I do agree with some of the statements with BTK and how he is gonna get caught. Other than than that the rest of the post illustrates the seemingly endless ability folks have reading hidden meaning in every word written whatever the meaning is. Apparently when the armchair PI get their feathers ruffled by people with opinions differing from theirs, the solution is to attack. Seeing hows according to them my postings are unnecssary until I have any other pertinent opinions I will keep them to myself, keeping the soothsayers and prognosticators pumping themselves up with self aggrandisement.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
